 ms event-loop timer plus the final interval through readiness. MaxPulseIntervalMs includes synchronous-ready work; P95 uses delivered pulses only. Outstanding jobs are sampled admitted work through decision delivery (including deferred ingress/local terminals), not continuous worker or CPU occupancy. Active-work keys record queue-to-event-filter delivery and queue-to-next-tick verified selection; no OS input-delivery clock is observed. The separate held-provider course observes continuous fixture entry, stop-token callback and provider exit on a steady clock; it models waiting work, not CPU occupancy. Active close measures the public close through whole-application quiescence, not stop-token acknowledgement. Measurement input gaps span consecutive 1 ms timer callbacks after native batching has started; initial publication delay remains in the phase timer. Wheel batch is measured after classification settles. CompositionStartupMs excludes process and QApplication launch. Responsiveness phase readiness includes synchronous QWidget rendering but excludes image encoding/writes; this is not display-compositor presentation or OS input-delivery latency. InputBudgetFailures retain unmet 100 ms phases; successful measurement does not accept them. The independent 1 ms all-zone live-heap sampler reports a lower-bound peak and its largest sample interval/cost; it cannot exclude unsampled peaks. No cross-platform latency budget."}
